    <briefdescription>
<para>Appends values to a pqxx::params and hands back the matching SQL placeholders. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Construction clears the supplied container, so each fresh <ref refid="structBase_1_1Binder" kindref="compound">Binder</ref> restarts numbering at $1 for one statement. Routing every value through <ref refid="structBase_1_1Binder_1a8fb0871ea4d994dfad3360aac44d8c56" kindref="member">bind()</ref> is what keeps callers from concatenating untrusted data into SQL text. <simplesect kind="note"><para>Holds a borrowed reference to the params container and must not outlive it. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>For a beginner: this is a helper struct that derived builders create on the stack for one SQL statement. It remembers a running counter so the first value becomes $1, the second $2, and so on, which is exactly what PostgreSQL expects in the prepared query. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
